    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is decided on the driver's own telemetry, and the outcome is the same on either side's account of who was where.\n\nA cancellation fee is chargeable only if all four conditions of POL-NS-01 hold. Conditions (a), (b) and (d) do hold: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 08:10:52; EV-GPS-00603 places the driver inside the 120 m large-venue arrival radius from 08:10:50 with 14 qualifying in-geofence fixes, so the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met; and the trip was terminated by the driver under the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW. Condition (c) fails. For a LARGE_VENUE pickup the driver must hold position inside the geofence continuously for 300 seconds, measured from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. The longest continuous in-geofence hold in the trace is 130 seconds (08:10:50 to 08:13:00), a shortfall of 170 seconds; the trip record's own wait_time_min of 2.3 minutes is consistent with that. The shortfall cannot be made up by summing separate intervals under POL-NS-06(i): the trace shows a single in-geofence interval (run_count 1), and EV-ADVIS-00603-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no qualifying traffic advisory exists to permit accumulation.\n\nBecause limb (c) fails, POL-NS-01 makes the fee not chargeable, and POL-NS-06 fixes the consequence as a full refund - expressly whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. That is the ruling, and the driver's advocate fairly conceded the arithmetic. The driver's explanation (five minutes, another booking queued) does not meet limb (c), which is a numeric test on the trace, not a matter of his convenience.\n\nOn the rider's further points: POL-NS-04 does not carry the case and is not needed. The driver placed an in-app voice call at 08:11:00, answered for 22 seconds, which defeats limb (b); and the chat log holds zero messages, so there is no locating or coordinating message for limb (a). The refund does not depend on that clause. The rider's own device track (32.6-40.6 m from the pin across 17 fixes, inside the 150 m large-venue presence radius) is consistent with her account of coming down, but it changes nothing, because POL-NS-06 refunds the fee regardless.\n\nOn the driver's points: the charge itself is arithmetically correct - SGD 4.00 is the greater of the SGD 4.00 LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee and the SGD 4.00 RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee, so the fare line reconciles under POL-NS-08(d) and there is no integrity defect. No false-arrival marker fired: at the arrival timestamp the driver was stationary inside the geofence, well under 300 m from the pin and below 15 km/h (distinct speeds top out at 8.8 km/h), so POL-NS-05 does not apply and no false-arrival referral is recorded against him.\n\nNo driver compensation is payable. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it; limb (c) fails and POL-NS-06 expressly provides that on a shortfall no driver compensation is payable. The anti-farming guard is never reached, and no referral arises.\n\nAmount: the contested line is the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee in EV-FARE-00603, charged (payment_status CHARGED) and unrefunded (refund_issued_sgd 0.00). A full refund of SGD 4.00 returns the whole contested amount to the filing rider.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact - the 170-second dwell shortfall - is carried by EV-GPS-00603 and EV-TRIP-00603, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, and the POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) show no impairment: no clock skew (arrival event 08:10:52 against a fix at 08:10:50), no trace gap (max_gap_sec 0.0, 45 fixes), a chat log consistent with the record's count of 0, and a fare line that reconciles. The MISSING advisory carries weight 0.0 and can carry no fact, but it is not the evidence for the deciding fact. Confidence is 0.95, above the 0.70 floor, and no POL-NS-09 escalation trigger applies."
