om POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 states that on a shortfall no driver compensation is payable, so the anti-farming guard is never reached. On the rider's POL-NS-04 point, the clause in fact does not apply — the chat log holds zero messages and the driver placed an answered 22-second in-app call at 08:11:00 — but the refund does not rest on it; it follows from the dwell shortfall alone. The rider's proximity track (32.6 to 40.6 m from the pin) is noted and is consistent with her account, but it is not the ground of decision. The trip record's wait_time_min of 2.3 and the 130-second trace are consistent with each other, and I have not recharacterised the driver's conduct as refusing the job: he arrived, held station and cancelled under the RIDER_NO_SHOW code, but cancelled 170 seconds before the waiting period the fee is consideration for had elapsed. Confidence is 0.95. The deciding facts are carried by EV-GPS-00603 and EV-TRIP-00603, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0; the only sub-1.0 artifact is the absent advisory, which carries no deciding fact. Nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) — the trace is 100 percent covered with a 0.0 s maximum gap and 45 driver fixes, the chat log's zero messages match trip_record.chat_message_count, and the fare line reconciles — so there is no POL-NS-09 trigger and no escalation. No clause produces a referral."
